1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,705
Two contexts. Different beans?

2
00:00:01,785 --> 00:00:02,940
Yes. Register alpha

3
00:00:02,940 --> 00:00:05,680
in context A, and beta in B.

4
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:07,020
Each independent context

5
00:00:07,020 --> 00:00:08,818
has its own registry.

6
00:00:08,898 --> 00:00:10,680
Context A finds alpha,

7
00:00:10,680 --> 00:00:12,440
but beta is missing.

8
00:00:12,440 --> 00:00:13,840
Sharing one Java application

9
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:16,071
doesn't connect these registries.

10
00:00:16,151 --> 00:00:18,060
Create a fresh parent and child.

11
00:00:18,060 --> 00:00:19,060
Set the parent before

12
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:20,560
refreshing the child.

13
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,311
The registries stay separate.

14
00:00:22,391 --> 00:00:24,360
The child checks locally first.

15
00:00:24,360 --> 00:00:25,380
A missing named bean

16
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:27,147
can be found in its parent.

17
00:00:27,227 --> 00:00:28,360
The parent cannot search

18
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:29,040
its children.

19
00:00:29,040 --> 00:00:31,900
Our tests confirm both directions:

20
00:00:31,900 --> 00:00:33,060
child to parent works;

21
00:00:33,060 --> 00:00:34,772
parent to child doesn't.

22
00:00:36,772 --> 00:00:37,862
Thanks for watching.

